    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362-a3">

                <pb facs="0522" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg426"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 189.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harris to Lake &amp; Co.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Nagasaki</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I am in receipt of yours of the 10th
                    instant, notifying me that you have been refused by the custom-house authorities
                    permission to load 300 sacks flour on the steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Adventure</hi>, and requesting me to make inquiries why you were refused
                    such permission. You <pb facs="0523" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/> inclose
                    application for export entry, showing that the flour was to be shipped to
                    uncertain points. Yesterday morning I had a personal interview with the
                    commissioner of customs, and he informed me that if the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Adventure</hi> will clear the port you will be allowed to load flour as you
                    request, but before you are granted that permission you must state in your
                    export entry application to what port the <hi rendition="#italic">Adventure</hi>
                    clears for.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles B. Harris</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
